# interactor-trailing-blank-on-ccl — three interactor tests fail on CCL

STATUS: open. Found 2026-08-28 while checking the compiler branch on the
CCL lane. NOT caused by the compiler work — see "Not from this branch".

## Symptom

`make test-ccl` fails three tests in INTERACTOR-SUITE, all with the same
shape: one extra `:BLANK` at the end of the input.

    MULTI-LINE-FORMS-READ-ACROSS-LINES
      ((+ 1 2) :BLANK) can't be destructured against (FORM):
      it contains 2 elements, and exactly 1 are expected.

    COMMA-COMMAND-READ-TAKES-SEXPS-EXCEPT-COMMA-LINES
      ((SETQ X 1) :BLANK #S(INPUT-COMMAND …)) against (SEXP CMD)

    COMMAND-READ-TAKES-LINES-AS-COMMANDS-EXCEPT-FORMS
      (#S(INPUT-COMMAND …) #S(INPUT-COMMAND …) (PRINT X) :BLANK :BLANK)
      against (CMD MOTION FORM BLANK)

`make test-sbcl` is green on all three. The whole rest of the corpus is
green on both.

## Repro

    make test-ccl

Or, smaller — the first failing test is:

    (read-all #'command-read (format nil "(+ 1~%   2)~%"))
    SBCL => ((+ 1 2))
    CCL  => ((+ 1 2) :BLANK)

## Where it comes from

All three failures go through the same path: a line is read, recognised
as the start of a Lisp form, pushed back with

    unread-line-from-input-context   (autolisp-interactor/source/input.lisp:24)

which replaces the context's stream by a CONCATENATED-STREAM of
[the line] + [a newline] + [the rest], and the form is then READ from
that stream.

What differs between the hosts is what is left in the stream after READ
returns, and therefore whether the NEXT `read-line` yields an empty line
(`:BLANK`) or `:EOF`. CCL leaves a trailing empty line where SBCL does
not.

That is a host difference in stream/READ behaviour, not a bug in either
implementation: the standard does not say whether READ consumes the
whitespace that terminated the object. The interactor's line reader is
simply written to one host's answer.

## Not from this branch

  - The compiler branch (2.0.1 .. 2.0.10) touches neither
    `autolisp-interactor/` nor `autolisp-reader/`:
    `git diff --stat <merge-base>..HEAD -- clautolisp/interactor
    clautolisp/autolisp-reader` is empty.
  - `autolisp-interactor/source/input.lisp` and its tests were last
    touched at 1.8.37, long before 2.0.
  - Nothing in the failure involves AutoLISP evaluation; it is Common
    Lisp READ on a string stream.

So this is longstanding, and the question worth answering is why the CCL
CI lane did not already show it — a different CCL version, or the lane
not actually running this suite. That is the first thing to check.

## Suggested fix

Do not depend on where READ left the stream. Two candidates:

  - After reading a form through an unread line, consume the rest of the
    current line explicitly (read to end-of-line and discard it if it is
    whitespace only). Deliberate rather than incidental, and identical on
    every host.
  - Or have the sexp path use a stream position it controls, instead of
    a CONCATENATED-STREAM whose EOF behaviour is what varies.

Either way the test to keep is the one that already caught it: reading a
multi-line form from a script ending in a newline must yield exactly the
forms, on every host.

## Why it matters now

GitLab CI is the source of truth and the CCL suite is one of its lanes,
so a red CCL lane blocks merging the compiler branch to master even
though the compiler is green on both hosts.
